# Electron Forge's system check refuses to run under pnpm unless `node-linker=hoisted` or an
# explicit hoist pattern is configured (@electron-forge/cli check-system.js): it assumes the
# packaged app needs a walkable `node_modules` tree, because most Forge apps ship their
# dependencies. This one does not — `dist/main.js` is a single esbuild bundle and
# `packagerConfig.ignore` (an allowlist) copies nothing but that file and package.json — so
# switching the whole workspace to a hoisted layout would be a large change made to satisfy a
# check that does not apply.
#
# Instead, state pnpm's OWN DEFAULT explicitly. `hoist-pattern[]=*` is exactly what pnpm already
# does (see `hoistPattern: ['*']` in the workspace's node_modules/.modules.yaml), so this file
# changes nothing about how anything installs; it only makes the value readable to
# `pnpm config get hoist-pattern`, which is what the check reads.
#
# Scope: pnpm reads a package-level .npmrc only when it runs with this directory as its cwd
# (`pnpm --filter @nex/shell …`, or Forge's own `pnpm config get`). A `pnpm install` at the
# workspace root does not see it — `pnpm config get hoist-pattern` from the repo root still
# prints `undefined`.
hoist-pattern[]=*
